njing, 210023, China."}]}}]}, "journalInfo": {"volume": "311", "journalIssueId": 4259883, "dateOfPublication": "2027 Jan", "monthOfPublication": 1, "yearOfPublication": 2027, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Talanta", "title": "Talanta", "essn": "1873-3573", "issn": "0039-9140", "isoabbreviation": "Talanta", "nlmid": "2984816R"}, "printPublicationDate": "2027-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2027", "pageInfo": "130299", "abstractText": "Creating a dual-target detection system capable of independent signal output holds potential for enhancing the analytical reliability of biomarker detection, which may aid in early-stage cancer screening. Herein, a nanozyme-catalyzed dual-potential electrochemiluminescence (ECL) immunosensor was described for the simultaneous detection of lung cancer biomarkers: carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) and neuron-specific enolase (NSE). Au-luminol functionalized CoFe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> nanoflowers (CoFe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub>@Au-luminol) served as the anodic probe, while CdS quantum dot-decorated hollow CeO<sub>2</sub> nanospheres (CeO<sub>2</sub>@CdS QDs) constituted the cathodic probe. CoFe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> and CeO<sub>2</sub> featuring multivalent elements (Co<sup>2+/3+</sup>, Fe<sup>2+/3+</sup>, Ce<sup>3+/4+</sup>), with their exceptional peroxidase (POD)-like activity, drove H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> co-reactant decomposition into abundant hydroxyl radicals (•OH) and superoxide anions (O<sub>2</sub><sup>•-</sup>), thereby boosting dual-potential ECL signals. Changes in the ECL responses at two different excitation potentials allowed CEA and NSE to be determined on the nanozyme-assisted immunosensor surface, respectively. The assay exhibited a linear range of 0.005-100 ng/mL, with detection limits of 0.87 pg/mL for CEA and 0.41 pg/mL for NSE. The nanozyme-enhanced ECL biosensing platform, characterized by superior specificity, stability, and practicability, offers significant potential for detecting multiple biomarkers.", "affiliation": "College of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering, Henan University of Technology, Zhengzhou, 450001, China. Electronic address: chencui@haut.edu.cn.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "Natural Science Foundation of Henan Province", "grantId": "242300420542", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Henan University of Technology", "grantId": "2021BS028", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Natural Science Foundation of China", "grantId": "22104030", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Nanjing University", "grantId": "SKLACLS2605", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Lung Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "BL", "qualifierName": "blood"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "DI", "qualifierName": "diagnosis"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Cadmium Compounds", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CH", "qualifierName": "chemistry"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Hydrogen Peroxide", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CH", "qualifierName": "chemistry"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Sulfides", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CH", "qualifierName": "chemistry"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Cerium", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CH", "qualifierName": "chemistry"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Cobalt", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CH", "qualifierName": "chemistry"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Gold", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbr